{"title":"2021 CJMC Problems/Problem 8","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_8\">Problem 8</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CJMC_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 8\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A square is broken up into smaller squares of side length 1, 2, 3, 4, or 5, as shown in the diagram. If a dart is thrown randomly at the square, what is the probability that it strikes one of the squares with side length 2?\n</p><p>(A) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/5/a659788d7a349117b319e617b859e6798553b5f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4}{81}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"24\" height=\"38\" />\n(B) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/0/5f0cf2a41ca6fbaafe3d21b823a9bed30c7272fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"20\" height=\"38\" />\n(C) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/3/283e0c63ce0c4c967db858f93e4876259f93f40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{6}{25}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"24\" height=\"38\" />\n(D) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/f/89f8914ddec472f71365684baa2221159248682b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4}{27}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" />\n(E) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/4/7547747b133453d3c209cff6cfbf129aa67a6947.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CJMC_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The overall side length of the large square is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/d/97d11df8924c8acbb10698d2b37b567e5051c453.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 + 4 = 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"76\" height=\"15\" />, giving a total area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/1/091a85fba0b5b9aecbf88d6ef3b8012db44f2432.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9^2 = 81$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"58\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>There are 3 squares with side length 2, contributing a total combined area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/6/b0644a24142d55013a8870d8be70b6dba8b8b5ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 \\times 2^2 = 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"92\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>The probability is:\n</p>\n<dl><dd><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/4/3e4c09143736e3744b8ef23d60fe2fa1e391234f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{12}{81} = \\frac{4}{27}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"70\" height=\"38\" /></dd></dl>\n<p><b>Answer:</b> <b>(D)</b>~prince_penguin_V\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CJMC_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CJMC_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2021 CJMC Problems/Problem 7\">Problem 7</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CJMC_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2021 CJMC Problems/Problem 9\">Problem 9</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018014815\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.008 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.010 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 53/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argum